Sval: about:home and about:newtab show Sval's home page

The about: module for both pages (AboutNewTabRedirector) builds its channel
from the activity stream's resource:// document, in the parent and in the
privileged content process alike. No pref selects another document, and a
chrome manifest override reaches only chrome:// URLs, so the one way to serve
Sval's page under those addresses is this getter. Everything else stays
Firefox's: the address bar still reads about:newtab, the preloaded new tab
still works, and the ContentSearch actor still attaches, which is what the
page searches through. about:privatebrowsing needs no patch: its address maps
to a chrome:// URL, which Sval's jar.mn overrides.

